      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change my answer, because the problem was never whether you meant to type 50 mg. The problems are that 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose and that the order isn't coming from a prescriber. The risk to the patient is the same however sure you are.\n\nHere is what can happen next:\n\n- **The prescriber enters it.** If the treating clinician wants a dose this far outside the label, they can review it with pharmacy and enter it themselves. They would take responsibility for that decision.\n- **I enter a standard dose.** A prescriber can confirm a dose of 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and I'll enter it right away. For example, they might choose 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **You pass on a concern.** If the patient has an urgent issue, such as severe hypertension, tell the treating team now. They can pick the right treatment."
      }
